id: pm-gh1598
title: "GH-1598: bind batch mutation APIs to PmClient and expose canonical staged preview records"
description: "GitHub https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1598 requests native PmClient preview/commit methods bound to host root and author policy, plus canonical staged records for idempotent intent comparison. Current staged preview validation remains shipped; its result contains validation state, constraints and warnings rather than complete staged records."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-26T04:54:51.880Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T22:07:25.991Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-28T22:07:25.021Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-28T22:07:25.021Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Expose typed PmClient previewItemMutations and commitItemMutations forwarding bound root and author policy to the existing SDK coordinator; Return per-mutation canonical staged ids, normalized metadata and bodies with generated-value provenance and explicit commit-time constraints; Prove preview/read-back equivalence for unchanged admitted plans and safe identical-intent replay versus typed changed-intent conflicts using native non-Git fixtures; preserve read-only previews and current guarded commit behavior"
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Implemented host-bound preview and commit methods with canonical final staged records, applied/adopted state, commit-time clock pointers and explicit replay constraints. Configuration-only bootstrap protects preview/status from optional-schema FIFO reads before staging."
expected_result: Packages can use SDK-owned normalized preview records and bound identity while preserving read-only preview and replay safety.
actual_result: "49/49 linked SDK/semantic-preview tests and full 11540-test exact-coverage run passed. Native unsafe-storage negative controls, type surface and Node/Bun packed artifact passed. Reviewed delivery is PR #1621; publication remains separate."
