comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T04:54:51.880Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict all-status corpus plus live request-specific searches and full terminal-lineage reads found no exact active owner. Existing SDK promotion and transaction/preview delivery remain completed; this item owns the newly requested public surface."
  "2026-10-28T19:44:10.177Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: typed root/author-bound PmClient preview and commit; canonical full staged item snapshots per executed mutation with explicit generated clock fields. Preserve committed replay semantics and read-only staging. Group with pm-gh1597 in one reviewed delivery; no other implementation items claimed."
  "2026-10-28T20:39:13.335Z","harness:codex","Validation: linked SDK plus semantic-preview integration tests passed 49/49. Staged records retain canonical body, normalized tags, author and provenance with explicit clock-field pointers, final-batch state and applied/adopted execution receipts. Committed replay returns no newly validated records. Public declaration tests and SDK surface snapshot are current. Full canonical coverage is running; the earlier 197-test focused coverage diagnostic retained the full-source denominator and is not a global coverage pass."
  "2026-10-28T21:08:13.590Z","harness:codex","Investigation and regression proof: the initial host wrapper activated extensions using hydrated source settings before safe preview setup. Native installed-package and isolated integration negative controls timed out on optional-schema and settings FIFOs. Configuration-only activation for preview/status fixes both before source reads; the same four unsafe-path fixtures then pass. This remains within host-bound preview ownership. The full candidate run completed 11539 passing tests with one 30-second timeout in existing literal-input coverage; no canonical coverage receipt was produced. Focused retry and hosted full coverage remain required."
  "2026-10-28T21:37:28.300Z","harness:codex",Recorded the real related relationship to the grouped recovery feature. The graph-composition gate detected that this delivery relationship existed only in prose; the typed edge now represents the shared host-bound transaction surface without inventing dependency or hierarchy depth.
  "2026-10-28T22:07:22.006Z","harness:codex","Final candidate validation: full sandboxed source coverage passed 11540 tests (3 platform skips), 880 passing files and 1 skipped file, with exact 71421/71421 statements, 55025/55025 branches, 14707/14707 functions and 67487/67487 lines. Linked recovery 65/65 and SDK/semantic-preview 49/49 passed, along with typecheck, ESLint, duplicate checks, generated contracts/surface/catalogs, docs links, graph composition and record integrity. Bounded mutation lane: 345 killed and 7 equivalent of 352, no failures. Final packed npm tarball passed Node and Bun batch/replay/retirement/replacement and unsafe-preview bootstrap controls. Local transport performance also failed unchanged base; thresholds remain unchanged and the initial PR head passed both hosted performance gates. Final revised head must pass hosted checks before merge. New APIs are not yet claimed as published."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T21:55:43.375Z","harness:codex","A read-only preview must protect the whole host bootstrap path, including configuration and extension setup. Staging guards alone are too late if bootstrap has already opened an optional-schema FIFO."
